{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Interpreted the s-c-d / s-c-s / s-c-s-m abbreviations as Spring Cloud Data Flow, Spring Cloud Stream, and Spring Cloud Stream Modules respectively, and the user stories as belonging to a single sprint that migrates XD-style capabilities into the SCDF/SCS ecosystem.",
    "HDFS sink (U1) will be implemented as a Spring Cloud Stream sink using Hadoop's FileSystem API with rolling file writers and configurable codecs, registered through the SCDF module registry.",
    "Hadoop shell commands (U2) will reuse the existing shell command SPI by adding a dedicated hadoop namespace that delegates to Hadoop's FileSystem shell commands (ls, cat, mkdir, copyFromLocal, etc.) executed through a mini-DFS or live cluster.",
    "Composed jobs (U3, U4) will be modeled as DAG definitions of job references; storage will be a relational JDBC repository (chosen after the U3 exploration spike) with a REST API for CRUD and lifecycle operations orchestrated by a new Composed Job Runner.",
    "Message property binding (U6) will be implemented as a SpEL-based binder extension that allows modules to declare inbound/outbound property-to-payload bindings declaratively in module configuration.",
    "JDBC (U7) and Kafka (U8) module migrations will copy the XD module code into the s-c-s-modules repository, adapt packaging and dependencies, convert them to standard Spring Cloud Stream source/sink conventions, and add isolated unit tests.",
    "Test coverage for shell commands (U5) will introduce a CommandTestFixture harness that mocks the deployment/runtime so shell commands can be unit-tested without spinning up a full stream."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer is senior, familiar with the Spring ecosystem (Spring Framework 6, Spring Cloud Stream, Spring Cloud Data Flow, Spring XD), and the existing SCDF module structure.",
    "An HDFS client (hadoop-client) and a Kafka client are already available on the classpath of the build; no infrastructure provisioning is required.",
    "A scratch HDFS instance (e.g. mini-DFS cluster) is available locally for tests, and a local Kafka broker is available for Kafka module tests.",
    "The U3 repository exploration is treated as a time-boxed spike that delivers a recommended approach plus a minimal prototype rather than a production-ready implementation.",
    "Composed jobs orchestration is a fresh design (no prior implementation to extend) and is limited to a sequential step DAG; branching, conditionals, and retries are not required for this increment.",
    "No localization, i18n, or UI work is included; the surface is Java modules, shell commands, and REST endpoints.",
    "Effort covers coding, unit/integration tests, and brief design notes; it excludes product management, code review cycles outside the developer, and ops/release engineering.",
    "All work is performed in the developer's home time zone, so estimates are pure development hours with no significant context-switch overhead."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Design HDFS sink module (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Define module metadata, configuration properties, partitioning strategy, and rolling-file semantics for the HDFS sink; produce a short design note.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement HDFS sink module (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Code the HDFS sink using Hadoop FileSystem API, handle output codec, file rolling, and error handling; wire it as a Spring Cloud Stream sink.",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Test HDFS sink module (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Add unit tests with a mini-DFS cluster and an integration test that exercises sink lifecycle, file rotation, and failure cases.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Design hadoop shell command namespace (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Decide the command grammar, options, and how the namespace will reuse the existing shell infrastructure.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Implement hadoop shell commands (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Add hadoop ls, cat, mkdir, copyFromLocal, copyToLocal, rm, and stat commands using Hadoop FileSystem and a configurable FileSystem URI.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Test hadoop shell commands (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Add unit tests using mini-DFS for each command, including error and permission edge cases.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Spike: explore repository options for composed jobs (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Investigate file-based, RDBMS, ZooKeeper, and in-memory options; evaluate trade-offs; produce a recommendation memo and a minimal JDBC-based prototype.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Design composed jobs orchestration (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Define the composed-job model (DAG of job references), execution semantics, lifecycle states, and REST API contract.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Implement composed job repository and runner (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the chosen JDBC repository, the ComposedJobRunner that launches jobs in sequence, the deployment listener, and the REST controller for CRUD and launch operations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Test composed jobs orchestration (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests for repository and runner, plus an integration test that launches a multi-job composed definition end-to-end on a local deployer.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Build CommandTestFixture harness (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Introduce a reusable test harness that wires up a shell command with mocked stream/runtime collaborators so commands can be exercised in isolation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Add isolated tests for existing shell commands (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Refactor existing shell commands to use the harness and add unit tests covering happy paths and error paths for each command.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "Design expression-based property binding (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Specify the binding DSL, the SpEL evaluation context, and how bindings integrate with Spring Cloud Stream channels and module configuration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "Implement property binding binder (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the binding engine that evaluates expressions on incoming/outgoing messages, applies transformations, and propagates results to module properties.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "Test property binding (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests for binding resolution, expression parsing, and integration tests verifying message property propagation across a sample module.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A16",
      "activity_name": "Migrate JDBC module to s-c-s-modules as sink (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Copy the XD jdbc module into s-c-s-modules, adapt packaging and Spring Cloud Stream sink conventions, update dependencies, and wire batch/single-write modes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A17",
      "activity_name": "Test migrated JDBC sink (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Add isolated unit tests using an in-memory DB and an integration test that writes stream payloads to JDBC.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A18",
      "activity_name": "Migrate Kafka module to s-c-s-modules as source (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Copy the XD kafka module into s-c-s-modules, adapt it to Spring Cloud Stream source conventions, and align consumer/producer configuration with binder properties.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A19",
      "activity_name": "Test migrated Kafka source (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Add unit tests with embedded Kafka and an integration test that reads messages from a topic and emits them on the source channel.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A20",
      "activity_name": "Module registry, documentation, and release prep",
      "activity_description": "Register the new and migrated modules in the SCDF module registry, update reference documentation and sample apps, and verify CI build and release notes for the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 180
  }
}
```

